## MerkleDb Erlang VM Arguments
## This file is evaluated at runtime.

## Name of the node
-name <%= @release.name %>@127.0.0.1

## Cookie for distributed erlang
-setcookie <%= @release.cookie %>

## Heartbeat management; auto-restarts VM if it dies or becomes unresponsive
## (Alarm, suspend, crash, etc. can cause this)
-heart

## Enable SMP (symmetric multi-processing)
-smp auto

## Number of async threads (default is 1, increase for I/O bound workloads)
+A 64

## Maximum number of atoms (default is 1M)
+t 2097152

## Maximum number of ETS tables
+e 65536

## Increase number of concurrent ports/sockets
-env ERL_MAX_PORTS 65536

## Increase number of concurrent processes (default is 262144)
+P 1048576

## Erlang scheduler configuration
## Bind schedulers to cores for better performance
+sbt db

## Dirty schedulers for NIFs (important for AVX2 operations)
+SDcpu 8:8
+SDio 16

## Memory allocator settings for high-throughput workloads
+MBas aobf
+MBscs 512
+MBlmbcs 1024

## Kernel poll (epoll on Linux, IOCP on Windows)
+K true

## Enable binary heap (more efficient for large binaries)
+hms 8192
+hmbs 8192

## Garbage collection settings
## Full sweep after 65535 collections
-env ERL_FULLSWEEP_AFTER 65535

## Enable crash dumps for debugging
-env ERL_CRASH_DUMP_SECONDS 30
-env ERL_CRASH_DUMP logs/erl_crash.dump

## Distribution buffer settings
+zdbbl 32768

## Time warp mode for accurate time keeping
+C multi_time_warp
